WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.347
Once the notebook version works, we can put a simple user interface around it.

00:00:05.347 --> 00:00:09.747
Streamlit is a convenient option for a class project.

00:00:09.747 --> 00:00:17.662
The interface asks for a question, calls our existing answer_question function, displays the answer,

00:00:17.662 --> 00:00:20.472
and then lists the retrieved sources.

00:00:20.472 --> 00:00:24.557
Notice that the UI does not reimplement RAG.

00:00:24.557 --> 00:00:29.492
The retrieval and generation logic stays in reusable functions.

00:00:29.492 --> 00:00:33.843
The application layer only collects input and displays output.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:38.802
That separation makes the code easier to test and maintain.

00:00:38.802 --> 00:00:42.312
I also recommend making the source panel visible.

00:00:42.312 --> 00:00:46.652
Users should be able to see where the answer came from.

00:00:46.652 --> 00:00:55.977
A polished RAG product may add authentication, feedback buttons, conversation history, tracing, or document links,

00:00:55.977 --> 00:00:59.427
but the basic app structure can remain simple.

00:00:59.427 --> 00:01:04.074
Build the pipeline first; add the interface after it works.
